From 9c58fa1888c619195e99b6ded939d250d0427cef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:48:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] host_loop_lease: one flock-held owner per Hermes
 home for host-wide background loops
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Infrastructure for design t_01a1d45d75851804 §2a (card t_01a1d470ec8f86ca); no loop is moved
onto it here.

hermes_cli/host_loop_lease.HostLoopLease(name, role, interval=...):
- flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB) on <realpath(root home)>/run/host-loops/<name>.lock (root home, so
  profile processes share one owner); fd O_CLOEXEC; the kernel frees it on death. A forked
  child closes its shared copy (never LOCK_UN, which would free the parent's lock).
- Holder metadata in the lock file: pid, start time, role, priority, core sha, heartbeat_at
  (beat() once per pass); released_at on release.
- Watchdog: no beat() for > 3x interval -> the holder releases; standbys log one WARNING per
  holder on a stale heartbeat.
- Priority gateway > serve > dashboard: a higher-priority standby writes <name>.want (pid +
  start, liveness-checked) and blocks on LOCK_EX in a daemon thread; the holder hands off in
  beat(); any other standby that wins the release window drops the lock again while a live
  .want of priority >= its own exists.
- held() costs one flock syscall when not holder (holder: none); kill switch
  HERMES_HOST_LOOP_LEASE=0 -> held() always True.
- Unopenable lock (no fcntl, uncreatable file, flock error) fails OPEN (held() True, logged
  once): duplicated passes are today's safe behaviour; failing closed would stop the loops.
  An existing read-only lock file is still locked through a read-only fd, as update_lock does.
- hermes doctor: "Host Loop Leases" lists each lease's holder (role, pid, core, beat age).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_host_loop_lease.py (real child processes: one holder of two,
kill -> standby within an interval, priority hand-off with a fast same-priority poller never
stealing, gateway never preempted by serve, wedged holder released by its watchdog, kill
switch, unwritable dir, read-only lock file, root-home key, stale warning once, doctor rows).
